## Workflow (version + changelog)

After any user-facing change to `Intonare.html`, or any shipped tool /
doc users or agents rely on for what shipped:

1. Bump the patch in both marketing declarations (HTML comment
   `INTONARE_VERSION:` and the JS `INTONARE_VERSION` const). Keep them
   equal.
2. Add a new top `## vX` entry in `CHANGELOG.md` in the same turn.
   Cover the whole batch of work, not a one-liner that skips half.
3. Do this before ending the task. Do not wait for Codemagic,
   TestFlight, or "when we ship." Codemagic still fails if top
   changelog and `INTONARE_VERSION` disagree; that is a backstop, not
   the first time you write the entry.
4. Tiny pure-internal agent scripts you delete in the same turn do not
   need a bump. Prototype labs under `tools/prototypes/` need a bump
   only when the change lands in the shipping app or a shipped audit.

## Do not

- Re-ask basics already covered here or in PROJECT_STATUS.
- Truncate or rewrite all of `Intonare.html` for a tiny change.
  If size collapses after an edit, restore that file from git first;
  never keep patching the truncated copy (see `intonare.mdc`).
- Run `release.bat` for everyday testing.
- Assume production is live on Play; closed testing until cutover.
- Assume Claude-era Python ship-gate scripts exist without checking
  `tools/README.md`. They are imported under `tools/` but need Python
  and a freshness pass before trusting pins.

